  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You guys should add syncing avatar triggers along with the new SDK3 system. They can be just like SDK2 world triggers, but more limited (probably only interact mode with things like SetGameObjectActive and others). These would be very very very nice! You could set them up so that they can either be activated by the owner only, by friend only, by all users, or by all users without syncing. This will allow users to make menus and UIs by activating and deactivating gameobjects by using trigger events! You could even make menus that change your animator controller states or toggle some objects and set blendshapes for things like clothing options. You can also make things such as an avatar soundboard that other users can click. The proximity needs to be limited so users cant make something that can be triggered from miles away and they could probably be turned off along with seats and animations. I feel like these can make great additions to avatars following or with the release of Avatar 3.0! They will also provide more power than Avatar 3.0 may initially provide, as from what I've seen, actions and moods might only be applicable to changing one state at a time or switching states, and would not allow for as much customization as this would.\n\ntl;dr:\n   these will allow you to make clickable buttons and objects on your avatar in order for you or others to manipulate it in interesting ways or even make a UI without any complex animator and/or particle contraptions.",
